In .NET MAUI, use the **lifecycle events** API in your `MauiProgram.cs` (or app builder configuration):

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // runs when app is paused
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // runs when app is no longer visible
        }));
#elif IOS
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app =>
        {
            // runs when app enters background
        }));
#endif
});
```

Make sure you have:
```csharp
using Microsoft.Maui.LifecycleEvents;
```

This uses platform-specific compiler directives (`#if ANDROID` / `#elif IOS`) so each handler only compiles for its target platform. You can chain multiple events (e.g., `.OnResume()`, `.WillEnterForeground()`) on the same builder.
